0company%20has%20been%20in%20talks%20with%20multiple%20legal%20software%20providers%20about%20introducing%20integrations.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EThe%20new%20release%20will%20test%20whether%20lawyers%20see%20ChatGPT%20as%20more%20than%20a%20helpful%20personal%20assistant.%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3E%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fopenai-enters-legal-ai-race-hires-jason-boehmig-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3EOpenAI%3C%2Fa%3E%20wants%20to%20sell%20large%20enterprises%20on%20its%20technology.%20Now%2C%20it's%20taking%20its%20case%20to%20law%20firms.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20ChatGPT%20maker%20is%20planning%20to%20launch%20new%20integrations%20with%20third-party%20legal%20software%20companies%2C%20according%20to%20people%20familiar%20with%20the%20matter.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAn%20OpenAI%20spokesperson%20declined%20to%20comment.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20company%20has%20been%20in%20talks%20with%20multiple%20legal%20software%20providers%20about%20allowing%20OpenAI's%20chatbot%20to%20plug%20into%20their%20tools%20and%20data%20sources%2C%20the%20people%20said.%20This%20way%2C%20lawyers%20could%20update%20a%20file%2C%20negotiate%20contracts%2C%20or%20search%20a%20legal%20database%2C%20without%20leaving%20ChatGPT.%20%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ELaw%20firms%20are%20under%20pressure%20from%20clients%20to%20move%20faster%20and%20show%20they're%20not%20billing%20associates%20for%20work%20that%20software%20can%20do.%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fin-house-legal-tech-ai-cost-cutting-2026-1%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3EIn-house%20legal%20teams%3C%2Fa%3E%20are%20looking%20for%20ways%20to%20automate%20more%20work%20themselves%2C%20so%20they%20can%20send%20less%20to%20outside%20counsel%20and%20shrink%20their%20legal%20bills.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThat%20demand%20has%20produced%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Flegal-tech-ai-startups-investors-funding-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eflood%20of%20startups%20addressing%20legal%20work%3C%2Fa%3E.%20For%20years%2C%20those%20companies%20have%20built%20on%20top%20of%20large%20language%20models%20supplied%20by%20frontier%20research%20labs%20such%20as%20OpenAI%20and%20Anthropic.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ENow%20the%20labs%20appear%20to%20want%20a%20closer%20relationship%20with%20the%20users%20themselves.%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fanthropic-expands-legal-ai-tools-claude-cowork-2026-5%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3EAnthropic%3C%2Fa%3E%20and%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fgoogle-unveils-gemini-enterprise-for-legal-law-tech-push-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3EGoogle%3C%2Fa%3E%20have%20both%20begun%20packaging%20their%20models%20as%20products%20for%20legal%20departments%20and%20law%20firms%2C%20selling%20directly%20to%20enterprises%20rather%20than%20only%20supplying%20the%20models%20themselves.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThat%20effort%20has%20been%20rippling%20through%20the%20public%20markets.%20Anthropic's%20February%20contract-review%20plugin%20helped%20ignite%20the%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fsoftware-stocks-ai-trade-tech-record-quarter-msft-orcl-intu-2026-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3E%26quot%3BSaaSpocalypse%2C%26quot%3B%3C%2Fa%3E%20a%20stock%20sell-off%20driven%20by%20fears%20that%20AI%20companies%20could%20absorb%20work%20once%20handled%20by%20stand-alone%20software.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EOpenAI%20enters%20the%20legal%20market%20with%20an%20unusual%20advantage.%20ChatGPT%20is%20already%20the%20best-known%20chatbot%20among%20the%20lawyers%20it%20hopes%20to%20win%20over.%20A%20%3Ca%20rel%3D%5C%22%20nofollow%5C%22%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.law360.com%2Fpulse%2Farticles%2F2454764%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3E%3Cu%3ELaw360%20survey%3C%2Fu%3E%3C%2Fa%3E%20found%20ChatGPT%20was%20the%20profession's%20most-used%20tool%2C%20with%2054%25%20of%20respondents%20reporting%20they%20use%20it%2C%20ahead%20of%20Microsoft%20Copilot%2C%20Gemini%2C%20Harvey%2C%20and%20Claude.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EBut%20the%20consumer%20brand%20is%20also%20a%20hurdle%20in%20a%20profession%20where%20confidentiality%20and%20precision%20are%20paramount.%20Lawyers%20may%20trust%20ChatGPT%20to%20plan%20their%20holidays%20in%20St.%20Barths.%20Persuading%20them%20that%20it%20belongs%20inside%20a%20firm's%20most%20sensitive%20workflows%20is%20another%20matter.%20Chatbots%20have%20already%20landed%20lawyers%20in%20hot%20water%20with%20judges%20for%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fai-hallucinations-court-filings-eve-dudley-debosier-2026-4%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Emaking%20up%20cases%3C%2Fa%3E%20and%20mangling%20their%20meanings.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20company%20is%20making%20its%20legal%20push%20three%20months%20after%20hiring%20Jason%20Boehmig%2C%20an%20executive%20who%20spent%20more%20than%20a%20decade%20figuring%20out%20the%20slow%2C%20messy%20business%20of%20selling%20software%20to%20lawyers.%20He%20had%20left%20a%20Big%20Law%20job%20to%20start%20Ironclad%2C%20a%20company%20that%20helps%20corporate%20legal%20departments%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fironclad-hits-200-million-arr-contract-lifecycle-management-ceo-2026-2%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Emanage%20contracts%3C%2Fa%3E.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ELawyers%20will%20be%20watching%20OpenAI's%20launch%20closely.%20The%20tech%20industry%2C%20meanwhile%2C%20is%20about%20to%20find%20out%20how%20much%20room%20the%20company%20intends%20to%20leave%20them.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fopenai-chatgpt-legal-ai-launch-2026-9%5C%22%3EBusiness%20Insider%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%22%2C%22published%22%3A1788467336000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a9969db3c906e69480d5b24%3Fformat%3Djpeg%22%2C%22originID%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fopenai-chatgpt-legal-ai-launch-2026-9%22%2C%22summary%22%3A%22OpenAI%20wants%20to%20sell%20large%